  "verified_against": {
    "source": "release-manifest.json",
    "agrees": true,
    "note": "Hashes were downloaded from the published v5.38.1 release assets and hashed independently, then checked again by re-fetching the URL this pin itself names. Only the pegasus artifact changed: install.sh and the two builder scripts are byte-identical to v5.28.0 and earlier. v5.38.1 corrects a report that v5.38.0 itself introduced, and the correction reaches this distribution directly because the report is what doctor prints to a person. v5.38.0 made doctor stop claiming a silent all-clear over ground it could not walk because a symlink stood in the way -- correct on its own -- but it recorded EVERY symlink it stepped over, including the ones that point at a regular file. On a real installation that is a dozen lines saying that whether there are orphaned empty directories underneath a cli.js cannot be said, and there is nothing underneath a file: the one case the report exists to surface was buried in noise. A skipped symlink is now recorded only when it resolves to a directory, which is the only way there can be unwalked ground under it. A link to a file, a dangling link and a self-referential loop are skipped exactly as before -- never walked into -- and no longer reported; a link to a directory is still skipped and still reported, unchanged. The defect was found by running v5.38.0 against a real installation, not by reading the code, and the engine's own review of the fix caught one guard that approved by a proxy another mechanism already provided, which was removed rather than kept. What v5.38.0 brought stands unchanged: an invalid granted_directories entry is quarantined instead of making the journal unreadable, and the repair command -- rendered under this distribution's own program name -- removes those entries and the empty directories doctor names, on an explicit request, with --dry-run and a snapshot taken first. This distribution changed nothing of its own for this pin beyond the alignment."
  }
}
